From: Alan Shearer
Subject: udp: free cloned buffer if DeliverData enqueue fails

DeliverData clones the incoming datagram, deframes it, then Enqueue()s
it. _Enqueue returns ENOBUFS when the socket receive buffer is full and
does not take ownership. EnqueueClone already frees on that failure;
DeliverData did not, so multicast/deliver_data to a full socket leaked
the clone.

---

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/udp/udp.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/udp/udp.cpp
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/udp/udp.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/udp/udp.cpp
@@ -1173,7 +1173,10 @@
 		return status;
 	}
 
-	return Enqueue(buffer);
+	status = Enqueue(buffer);
+	if (status != B_OK)
+		gBufferModule->free(buffer);
+	return status;
 }
 
 
